<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Cenel Loairn</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 850 CE (approx.) · capital Dunollie</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A leading kindred of Dal Riata in northern Argyll, rivals of Cenel nGabrain, whose descendants may later have ruled Moray.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cenel Loairn claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loarn-mac-eirc">Loarn mac Eirc</a>, said to be a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergus-mor">Fergus Mor</a>, the legendary founder of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata</a>. By the 7th century it controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorn">Lorn</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isle-of-mull">Mull</a> and neighbouring districts in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, with its main stronghold at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunollie">Dunollie</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oban">Oban</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other Dal Riatan kindreds it owed naval service and tribute recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senchus-fer-n-alban">Senchus fer nAlban</a>. Its kings competed with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cenel-ngabrain">Cenel nGabrain</a> for the kingship of all <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata</a>, and in the late 7th and early 8th centuries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferchar-fota">Ferchar Fota</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selbach-mac-ferchair">Selbach</a> held that position. Selbach burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunollie">Dunollie</a> in 701 and later rebuilt it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selbach-mac-ferchair">Selbach</a>'s defeat at sea in 719 and Pictish conquest under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oengus-i-of-the-picts">Oengus son of Fergus</a> in the 730s broke Cenel Loairn's power. Later Scottish genealogies traced the rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-moray">Kingdom of Moray</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macbeth-king-of-scotland">Macbeth</a>, to this kindred, though the link is debated.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cenel-loairn.jpg" alt="Cenel Loairn" width="320" height="340"><figcaption>Image: Kelisi at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FirthofLornmap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dunollie</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ferchar Fota, Selbach mac Ferchair</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cenél Loairn</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=cenel-loairn" aria-label="Cenel Loairn on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4671 317 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cenel Loairn lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4991 573L4881 524M4991 573L4909 487"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 524h0M4909 487h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4991 573h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4991 573h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dunollie. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=cenel-loairn">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
